A Sonnet on Software Engineering

When logic flows through circuits yet unseen,
And algorithms dance in perfect time,
We craft the systems that have come to mean
The bridge between the abstract and sublime.

Each line of code, a brick within the wall,
Each function built with purpose, clean, and true,
We debug through the night, we heed the call,
To build what users never thought they'd do.

Through testing, refactoring, and review,
We shape the digital world, line by line,
Where problems vast are broken down anew,
And elegant solutions brightly shine.

So here's to those who code with heart and mind,
The engineers who leave the world refined.
